  "research_id": "route-anchor-inventory",
  "title": "Route–Anchor–Inventory — Private Dollar Rails and Adoption Gates",
  "question": "Is the monetary transition better understood as functional unbundling in which private routes and operating forms expand while the dollar and sovereign institutions retain the anchor, liquidity and failure layers, and what separate GENIUS, agentic-payment, post-quantum and persistent-inventory receipts would establish that architecture?",
  "bluf": "The likely monetary transition is functional unbundling rather than fiat replacement: the dollar remains the denomination and sovereign anchor; regulated stablecoins and tokenized deposits become operating forms; private adapters and specialized ledgers select and execute routes; liquidity providers maintain working inventory; and the Fed, banks, market utilities and courts remain concentrated at account access, authoritative record, residual settlement, correction and crisis liquidity. GENIUS supplies the legal-claim gate, agentic systems supply delegated demand and route abstraction, and post-quantum migration supplies the durability gate. XRP captures a distinct role only if it repeatedly wins permitted conversion routes and creates persistent institutional inventory.",
  "evidence_cutoff": "2026-08-31T14:43:21-04:00",
  "evidence_cutoff_note": "User-reviewed working thesis plus a primary-linked implementation audit through the cutoff. G7/G20, Overall DLT, Federal Reserve, GENIUS, private-stack, network and company packages remain the component owners. No vault event, canonical watch, plotline, forecast or installed-app shipment is created.",
  "use_note": "The factual matrix carries primary links and bounded negatives. The cross-system synthesis remains a working hypothesis and is not evidence of coordinated timing, completed adoption, native-token value capture or a price implication.",
